MAIN ARCHITECTURE CONCEPTS YOU'LL LEARN:

Serverless
- AWS runs the compute for you.

Scalability
- Resources can handle increasing traffic.

Decoupling
- Services don't need to depend directly on each other.

High Availability
- Design systems to continue working if part of the infrastructure
  fails.

Security
- Control access using IAM, security groups, private networks, etc.

Networking
- Control how AWS resources communicate with each other and the
  internet.

Caching
- Store frequently requested data closer to users to reduce latency
  and backend load.

Event-Driven Architecture
- One event can trigger actions across multiple services.
